 "final_message": "Application BHL-26001 for 14 Larch Lane is submitted, the lender's condition is answered, and Brightpath has recorded your intent to proceed.\n\n- **Documents:** I uploaded only the August and September statements for Sam's Juniper checking and savings and Nadia's Northgate checking and savings. I also uploaded the last two Larkspur payslips for each of you. I left Nadia's business account alone.\n- **Application:** I filled in your profile, employment and the four account balances, and got the loan details from your instructions. Gross monthly pay is Sam $8,016.67 and Nadia $7,366.67, which is each annual salary divided by 12. I gave the credit-check and e-sign consents and submitted once.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The lender asked about the $8,000 deposit on 9/3 into Sam's Juniper checking. I asked you, and sent your answer that it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan.\n- **Loan Estimate:** It came in under all three limits, so I signed the intent to proceed with both your names.\n\n| | Estimate | Your limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | 6.25% | 6.5% |\n| Monthly payment | $3,042.41 | $3,100 |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 |\n\nThe estimated cash to close is $122,850, and the rate lock is available for 45 days. The lender hasn't said whether it accepted the explanation of the deposit, so that is the next thing to watch.",
